// Professor Oak: greets new trainers and hands them over to the starter selection (art-fixes)
NPCs.ProfessorOak: {
	DisplayName: Professor Oak

	Dialogue: {
		Intro1: Hello there, {0}! Welcome to the world of Pokémon! My name is Oak. People call me the Pokémon Professor.
		Intro2: This world is inhabited far and wide by creatures called Pokémon! They live in every biome: forests, deserts, snow, caves, the ocean... Explore, and you'll keep finding new ones.
		Intro3: To catch a wild Pokémon, throw a Poké Ball at it. Some will put up a fight, so don't give up after one miss!
		Intro4: The Gym Leaders are waiting for you too. Defeat the great bosses of this world and they'll accept your challenge, with a Gym Badge for whoever wins.
		Intro5: Press {1} to see the Summary of your Pokémon, and {2} to open your Pokédex. Completing it is my dream... will you help me fill its pages?
		Intro6: But first, every trainer needs a partner. I have some Pokémon here with me. Go on, choose one!
		StillChoosing: Ah, {0}! Still deciding? Take your time. A first partner is a friend for life!
		Tip1: Different Pokémon live in different biomes. If one is hard to find, try exploring somewhere new!
		Tip2: Great Balls and Ultra Balls catch Pokémon more easily than a regular Poké Ball. Worth every coin!
		Tip3: Your Pokémon can hold an item. Leftovers or an Oran Berry can keep them going in a tough battle.
		Tip4: Brock, the Pewter City Gym Leader, accepts challengers once the Eye of Cthulhu has been defeated.
		Tip5: Press {0} to check a Pokémon's Summary: its stats, moves, nature and more.
		Tip6: Every Pokémon you see or catch is recorded in your Pokédex. Press {1} to open it.
		Tip7: Pokémon grow stronger by battling, and many of them evolve. I can't wait to see yours!
		NextButton: Next
		SkipButton: Skip
		ChooseButton: Choose my partner!
		ThanksButton: Thanks, Professor!
		TipButton: Any tips?
		AgainButton: Tell me again
		Unbound: (no key set)
	}
}
